# K18 guard corpus — THE {0,2} SPLIT-SHAPE FAMILY (docs/design/k18_memo_design.md
# §2b, §5 item 1; docs/dev/known_issues.md K18, FIXED 2026-08-15).
#
# These 83 patterns are the design lane's central result, and they are here
# because they are the sub-case an acceptance corpus derived from K18's own
# witnesses cannot reach. A two-line candidate repair (B: walk THROUGH an
# already-seen ordinary epsilon state instead of dying there) passes all 165
# cases of the acceptance corpus and is still wrong. Over a dense
# 18,858-pattern shape sweep it differs from the landed repair on exactly
# these 83 patterns / 98 cells, and python3 `re` agrees with the landed repair
# on 98 of 98 and with B on 0.
#
# Every one has a `{0,2}`-quantified body: the conflation happens at a nested
# optional SPLIT rather than at an N_EPS, which is a THIRD sub-case of the
# root fact (a per-closure memo keyed on the NFA state alone, against an
# empty-iteration rule that is a property of the walk's own path). Passing the
# 165 is not an acceptance criterion for this class; these are.
#
# Every expectation generated from python3 `re` AND libpcre2 10.46, both
# oracles agreeing on every cell (D44's three-way rule).

pattern (?:(?:b*|a){0,2})*
m "" 0 0
m "a" 0 0
m "b" 0 1
m "aa" 0 0
m "ab" 0 0
m "ba" 0 1
m "bb" 0 2
m "aab" 0 0
m "bab" 0 1
m "aba" 0 0
m "abab" 0 0
m "aabb" 0 0

